# software-economics

Apply the software-economics skill when the request matches its scope.

Capabilities:
- model software TCO across build, buy, open source, and migration alternatives
- quantify cost of delay, cost of quality, technical debt economics, lock-in, and option value
- compare alternatives using unit economics, scenarios, sensitivity, and decision thresholds
- produce and validate a SoftwareEconomicsArtifact with traceable assumptions and evidence

Stop when: Alternatives, horizon, cost drivers, demand, delay, quality/debt effects, lock-in and option assumptions are explicit; calculations reconcile; sensitivity exposes decision reversals; the SoftwareEconomicsArtifact validates or is marked blocked with schema errors.
